{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["Which fields do you truly need before handing over the file, and which could you learn later?","Is a work email worth the downloads it will cost you, given who reads this guide?","What happens to someone who asks for a call, and who owns that reply?","Does the consent wording match what you will actually send?"],"howToUseResponses":"Sort responses by the reason people gave. Readers researching a purchase who asked for a call are sales conversations, so pass them on the same day with their timeline. The problems people describe are a list of topics for your next guide, and the learning focus answers show which part of the subject pulls readers in. Only email people who agreed to hear more.","customizeSteps":["Change the greeting and endings to name the guide, and add its download link to both endings or send it from your own email as responses come in.","Decide whether to keep the work email rule, and trim the role list to the people you write for.","Embed the form on the landing page for the guide, and export the responses to CSV to see which reasons bring in the most readers."],"faqs":[{"q":"What is gated content?","a":"Content such as an ebook, report or checklist that visitors get in exchange for filling in a short form. It is a common way to turn readers into leads."},{"q":"How many fields should a gated content form have?","a":"As few as you can manage. An email and a name are often enough, and every extra required field loses some readers, so this form keeps the qualifying questions to the people who are researching a purchase."},{"q":"Should I ask for a work email to download content?","a":"It helps if you sell to businesses and want better leads, but it costs downloads from freelancers and students. Turn it off in the email question if reach matters more than qualification."},{"q":"Do people who download content consent to marketing emails?","a":"Not automatically. This form asks separately and lets people say no, so you only email readers who agreed."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":10,"title":"Content download","description":"Gate a guide without making it feel like a toll booth.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_contentd00","ref":"welcome","title":"Your guide is nearly ready. Tell us where to send it.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_contentd01","ref":"email","title":"What's your work email?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"email","unique":false,"businessOnly":true,"allowedDomains":[],"verify":false},{"id":"blk_contentd02","ref":"name","title":"And your first name?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique":false,"minLength":0,"maxLength":80},{"id":"blk_contentd03","ref":"company","title":"Which company are you with?","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique":false,"minLength":0,"maxLength":150},{"id":"blk_contentd04","ref":"role","title":"Which best describes your role?","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"dropdown","options":[{"id":"opt_founder_or_owner","label":"Founder or owner","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_manager_or_team","label":"Manager or team lead","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_individual_contributor","label":"Individual contributor","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_consultant_or_agency","label":"Consultant or agency","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_student","label":"Student","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_other","label":"Other","image_key":null}]},{"id":"blk_contentd05","ref":"interest","title":"What brought you to this guide?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_researching_a_purchase","label":"Researching a purchase","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_solving_a_speci